 "note": "One of five independent 500-image draws from COCO val2014, used to measure how much CHAIR moves when only the image set changes. This matters because the released char_eval.py takes os.listdir() of an unpublished directory (/data-disk/only_test), shuffles it and keeps the first 500 -- so WHICH 500 the paper scored depends on that directory's contents and on filesystem order, and is not recoverable. Our CHAIR baseline sits 3.88 points from the paper's while our POPE baseline, which uses POPE's fixed official files, sits 0.05 from it. These draws test whether the image set accounts for that."
